    {
      "id": "d2",
      "title": "Guard once in the shared business layer, not per adapter",
      "source": "author",
      "chose": "Put the check in OrderSubscription, which every adapter funnels through.",
      "rejected": "Validate in each adapter — queue handlers, the poller, the linked-record fetch",
      "why": "The unsafe cast happens in several adapters, but they all converge on the subscription before business logic runs. One choke point covers every entry point — created, updated, cancelled, fulfilled, refunded — instead of scattering the same validation and missing one.",
      "quote": "OrderSubscription — the single business layer all adapters funnel through — now skips records with an unrecognized category at every entry point.",
      "quoteSrc": "PR description · Change",
      "evidence": [
