      "id": "d5",
      "title": "Leave the exhaustive switch as an unreachable invariant",
      "source": "author",
      "chose": "Keep categoryLabel's throwing switch untouched.",
      "rejected": "Add a default arm to absorb unknown values",
      "why": "The upstream guard means the switch can no longer be reached with a bad value. Softening it with a default would silently absorb future real bugs; keeping it strict documents the invariant 'everything reaching here is recognized' and still throws loudly if a different path ever breaks that.",
      "quote": "The exhaustive switch in categoryLabel is left as-is (now an unreachable defensive invariant).",
      "quoteSrc": "PR description · Change",
      "note": "A deliberate non-change — invisible in the diff.",
