    {
      "id": "d6",
      "title": "Count null as a recognized category",
      "source": "infer",
      "chose": "Include null in the recognized set, so it processes normally.",
      "rejected": "Treat null as unrecognized and skip it too",
      "why": "null is a legitimate member of OrderCategory ('no specific category'), distinct from the sentinel string signalling an out-of-union value. Skipping null would drop valid records that simply have no category assigned.",
      "inferNote": "The code marks null as recognized with an inline comment, but the reasoning — that null is a valid domain value unlike the sentinel — is reconstructed from the type definition. The PR body doesn't discuss null, and the rejected alternative is illustrative.",
